# xFinance Branding — Production Rules for Cursor

**Reference (Grok one-slide review & scaling feedback)**  
Narrative alignment: [xFinance One-Slide Review & Scaling Feedback (shared Grok)](https://grok.com/share/bGVnYWN5LWNvcHk_d2f3a353-3fe4-4fa9-a5d8-f6ff41642993).  
When the share and this rule disagree, **this rule + repo implementation** win; refresh the rule if the Grok thread updates.

**Core Positioning (use everywhere)**
- Tagline: **"No Atoms Moved. Just Gains Earned."**
- Subline: **"Cheapest xFinance at $2/hr • Options Profits Powered by Grok"**
- Promise: Turn options into daily gains (covered calls, protective puts, straddles, unified scanner). Zero fluff. Institutional tools at retail price.
- **One-slide discipline:** Lead with outcome (gains / defined-risk options income), then stack (portfolio → xChat → exam/coach), then proof ($2/hr, pay-per-use). Avoid feature dumps before the hook.

**Differentiation (investor + GTM — current state)**
- **Bundle:** Execution-style portfolio tools + **advisory chat (Grok / xAI)** + **exam prep (xCoach)** in **one workspace** — a rare combination vs point-solution chatbots or read-only dashboards alone.
- **MVP priority (perceived value):** Ship **xChat** + **basic portfolio tracking** first; advisory runs on **Grok API** / xAI Responses. Layer xCoach and deeper execution as the stack matures.

**Honest weak spots (copy & creative — fix over time)**
- Avoid **early-stage** vibes: “stub”, “picker shipping now”, generic “start free — upgrade” **without** proof. Prefer concrete outcomes and dark-launch / access clarity.
- **Not yet in product:** Live usage metrics, customer testimonials, rich proof-of-concept visuals — do **not** invent them; use “approved access”, “waitlist”, or roadmap language until shipped.

**GTM, partnerships & waitlist (targets)**
- **Near-term goal:** **~1k signups in 30 days** to validate demand before heavy build — frame as **waitlist / early access**, not mass-market scale claims.
- **Channels:** FinTwit / finance X; HNWI & trusted-family wealth pros; **Series 7 / 65 / 66** candidates on LinkedIn & Reddit.
- **Partnerships:** Finance influencers for **early-access reviews** — offer clear narrative: bundle + Grok advisory + compliance-forward positioning.
- **Waitlist landing:** Use the **one-slide / hero** story (differentiation + $2/hr + product stack); single CTA to join waitlist; optional credential step below.

**Compliance narrative (trust, not legal advice)**
- Emphasize **for approved professionals** and **controlled access** — aligns with dark-launch and Admin → Access flows.
- **Roadmap:** Waitlist can mention **credential upload (FINRA / SEC)** to filter serious users — **only when productized**; never fake a flow in UI. Copy stays “not financial advice” where disclaimers exist (e.g. xChat footer).

**Monetization: roadmap vs pricing lock-in**
- **Shipped / canonical customer UI:** **$2/hr** usage + tooltip (Pricing Lock-in below) — do not remove from primary surfaces without an explicit product change.
- **Investor & deck roadmap:** **Freemium → tiered subscriptions** (illustrative: **~$29/mo** advisor tier, **~$99/mo** full execution + coach) — use in **investor decks**, waitlist **secondary** copy, or `/plans` when implemented. If both appear, lead with **$2/hr** transparency, then tiers as “also available” or “coming”.

**Visual Identity (lightning + green cyber-finance vibe)**
- **Logo lockup (mandatory):** **aTx** (gain-green, `--xf-gain-green`) + **⚡** (lightning bolt, **`--xf-lightning-yellow`**) + **Finance** (white) = **aTx⚡Finance**. Do not drop the bolt between **aTx** and **Finance** in the wordmark. Code: `src/app/ui/atxfinance-logo.tsx` (`AtxFinanceMark`, `LightningBolt`, span).
- **Primary Icon (standalone / heroes):** Lightning ⚡ + stylized **xF** where a full lockup is not used (e.g. large marketing marks).
- **Color Palette:**
  - Background: `#050505` (pure black like xAI API)
  - Accent Green: `#22c55e` (neon gains — marketing hero); app surfaces also use `--xf-gain-green` (#39ff14) per brand kit
  - Text: `#f1f5f9` / `#94a3b8`
  - Lightning Yellow highlight: `#eab308` on hover
- **Typography:**
  - Heading: `font-bold tracking-tighter text-5xl md:text-7xl` (Inter or system-ui)
  - Sub: `font-medium text-2xl text-emerald-400`
  - Body: `font-mono text-sm text-slate-400` for financial data
  - Tagline: `font-black uppercase tracking-[4px] text-emerald-400`

**Product Hierarchy**
- xFinance → Core portfolio + scanners
- xChat → AI advisor (Grok / xAI-backed)
- xCoach → Learning / exam readiness
- xMoney → Coming soon (execution / money movement)

**Scaling narrative (copy-level, not infra)**
- **Usage-based:** $2/hr, pay only for what you use — say it near every primary CTA.
- **Trust path:** Dark-launch / access workflow is a feature, not an apology; approved users first.
- **Heavy workloads:** Batch / async flows (e.g. xChat batch) are “scale without pretending everything is real-time.”
- **Governance:** Personas, plans, and audit trails support scaling teams without diluting the retail story.

**Pricing Lock-in**
- Every page, every button, every hero must show **"$2/hr"** in emerald-400 with tooltip: "Cheapest xFinance on earth — pay only for what you use."

**When to use this rule**
- Any new page/component with xFinance, xChat, xCoach, xMoney
- Hero sections, nav, chat header, pricing cards
- One-pagers, investor or partner-facing blurbs, **waitlist landings**, and “single slide” exports

**Strict Rules**
- Use **aTx⚡Finance** (wordmark), **aTxFinance**, or **xFinance** in user-facing copy as appropriate; technical identifiers (`atxfinance` tool type, env vars, DB names) may remain.
- Always green **"Gains Earned"** highlight.
- Dark mode only. No light theme.
- Every recommendation must tie back to options profit (covered calls, protective puts, unified scanner).

**Design system (source of truth)**
- Use `--xf-*` tokens from `atx-docs/design-system/atxfinance-brand-kit.css`. No hardcoded hex in app CSS.
- Accent green: `--xf-gain-green` (#39ff14). Marketing hero may use `emerald-400` (#22c55e) per design review — see `atx-docs/xchat/xfinance-branding-review.md`.

**When user says "xFinance branding", "new hero", or "investor / waitlist slide"**
- Output a Tailwind component using `--xf-*` tokens, tagline, subline, **$2/hr**, product hierarchy (xFinance, xChat, xCoach, xMoney), **aTx⚡Finance** lockup (bolt between aTx and Finance), and **differentiation** (execution + advisory + exam prep in one place). For waitlist/investor context, add a **secondary** line on early access / professionals / roadmap tiers without inventing metrics or testimonials.
